IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 — WORKING DAYS.
--
-- s 5 defines "working day" (the same days as the Legislation Act 2019,
-- s 13); s 55 of that Act extends periods ending on other days.

§ `Working days`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- The Gregorian computus (Meeus, Jones and Butcher) for Easter Sunday.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Easter Sunday in` y MEANS
    Date (((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) MODULO 31) PLUS 1) (FLOOR ((h PLUS l MINUS (7 TIMES m) PLUS 114) DIVIDED BY 31)) y
    WHERE
        a MEANS y MODULO 19
        b MEANS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        c MEANS y MODULO 100
        d MEANS FLOOR (b DIVIDED BY 4)
        e MEANS b MODULO 4
        f MEANS FLOOR ((b PLUS 8) DIVIDED BY 25)
        g MEANS FLOOR ((b MINUS f PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 3)
        h MEANS ((19 TIMES a) PLUS b MINUS d MINUS g PLUS 15) MODULO 30
        i MEANS FLOOR (c DIVIDED BY 4)
        k MEANS c MODULO 4
        l MEANS (32 PLUS (2 TIMES e) PLUS (2 TIMES i) MINUS h MINUS k) MODULO 7
        m MEANS FLOOR ((a PLUS (11 TIMES h) PLUS (22 TIMES l)) DIVIDED BY 451)

GIVEN month IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first Monday of month` month `in` y MEANS
    Date (1 PLUS ((8 MINUS `Weekday of` (Date 1 month y)) MODULO 7)) month y

-- s 5 (as Legislation Act 2019, s 13): "working day means a day of a week other than—
-- (a) a Saturday, a Sunday, Waitangi Day, Good Friday, Easter Monday, Anzac
-- Day, the Sovereign's birthday, Te Rā Aro ki a Matariki/Matariki Observance
-- Day, and Labour Day; and (b) a day in the period commencing with 25
-- December in a year and ending with 2 January in the following year; and
-- (c) if 1 January falls on a Friday, the following Monday; and (d) if 1
-- January falls on a Saturday or a Sunday, the following Monday and Tuesday;
-- and (e) if Waitangi Day or Anzac Day falls on a Saturday or a Sunday, the
-- following Monday". Matariki Observance Days are an input.
@ref s 5 working day
@export Whether a day is a working day under s 5 of the Credit Contracts and Consumer Finance Act 2003 (NZ): not a weekend, Waitangi Day, Good Friday, Easter Monday, Anzac Day, the Sovereign's birthday, Matariki Observance Day or Labour Day; not 25 December to 2 January; and not the Monday (and Tuesday) after a 1 January that falls on a Friday (or weekend), or the Monday after a weekend Waitangi Day or Anzac Day. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A DATE  @desc The day
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a working day` d `, Matariki days` matariki IF
        NOT w EQUALS Saturday
    AND NOT w EQUALS Sunday
    AND NOT mondayised (Date 6 2 y)
    AND NOT mondayised (Date 25 4 y)
    AND NOT d EQUALS `the day` (0 MINUS 2) `days after` easter
    AND NOT d EQUALS `the day` 1 `days after` easter
    AND NOT d EQUALS `the first Monday of month` 6 `in` y
    AND NOT d EQUALS `the day` 21 `days after` (`the first Monday of month` 10 `in` y)
    AND NOT elem d matariki
    AND NOT (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY d AT LEAST 25)
    AND NOT (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY d AT MOST 2)
    AND NOT (newYear EQUALS Friday AND d EQUALS Date 4 1 y)
    AND NOT (newYear EQUALS Saturday AND (d EQUALS Date 3 1 y OR d EQUALS Date 4 1 y))
    AND NOT (newYear EQUALS Sunday AND (d EQUALS Date 3 1 y OR d EQUALS Date 4 1 y))
    WHERE
        w MEANS `Weekday of` d
        y MEANS DATE_YEAR d
        easter MEANS `Easter Sunday in` y
        newYear MEANS `Weekday of` (Date 1 1 y)
        GIVEN holiday IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        mondayised holiday MEANS
               d EQUALS holiday
            OR (`Weekday of` holiday EQUALS Saturday AND d EQUALS `the day` 2 `days after` holiday)
            OR (`Weekday of` holiday EQUALS Sunday AND d EQUALS `the day` 1 `days after` holiday)

-- The n-th working day after a date ("within n working days after").
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the` n `th working day after` d `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF   `is a working day` next `, Matariki days` matariki
         THEN `the` (n MINUS 1) `th working day after` next `, Matariki days` matariki
         ELSE `the` n `th working day after` next `, Matariki days` matariki
    WHERE
        next MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` d

-- Legislation Act 2019, s 55: "A thing that, under legislation, must or may
-- be done on a particular day or within a limited period of time may, if that
-- day or the last day of that period is not a working day, be done on the next
-- working day".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 55
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` d `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    IF   `is a working day` d `, Matariki days` matariki
    THEN d
    ELSE `the` 1 `th working day after` d `, Matariki days` matariki

-- Legislation Act 2019, s 56: a period of n months "(a) starts at the start of
-- the relevant day in the month; and (b) the relevant number of months must
-- then be counted to find the ending month; and (c) the period ends
-- immediately before the corresponding day in the ending month or (if there
-- is no such day) at the close of the last day of the ending month" (added
-- after the independent pass).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 56
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of` n `months beginning with` d MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY d
    THEN `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` target
    ELSE target
    WHERE
        target MEANS `add months` d n
